.TH DIFFA-SNAPSHOT 1 "November 2025" "diffa 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffa\-snapshot \- create a snapshot of a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffa snapshot
\fIDIRECTORY\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a snapshot of a directory structure, storing file paths, sizes, modification times, and content hashes in a SQLite database. Snapshots capture the state of a directory without storing actual file content, making them lightweight and efficient for large directory structures.
.PP
Snapshots can be used for:
.IP \(bu 2
Directory comparison (current vs historical state)
.IP \(bu 2
Change detection and integrity monitoring
.IP \(bu 2
Build verification
.IP \(bu 2
Patch creation without requiring both directories
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Output snapshot file path (required). Use .diffa extension
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-symlinks
Follow symbolic links instead of storing them as-is (default: don't follow)
.TP
.B \-\-exclude \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude files matching pattern (can be repeated). Supports wildcards (*.log, temp/*, etc.)
.TP
.B \-\-use\-cache
Enable hash caching for faster subsequent scans of the same directory
.TP
.B \-\-parallel
Enable parallel hashing for faster processing on multi-core systems
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a basic snapshot:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa snapshot /path/to/dir \-o snapshot.diffa
.fi
.RE
.PP
Snapshot with exclusions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa snapshot /project \-o project.snapshot \\
  \-\-exclude "*.log" \-\-exclude ".git/*"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fast snapshot with parallel hashing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
diffa snapshot /large\-dir \-o large.diffa \-\-parallel \-\-use\-cache
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
The command displays:
.IP \(bu 2
Progress during snapshot creation
.IP \(bu 2
Final statistics: file count, directory count, total size
.IP \(bu 2
Duration of the operation
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (missing required argument)
.TP
.B 3
File system error (directory not found, permission denied)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I OUTPUT.diffa
SQLite database containing directory structure, file metadata, and content hashes
.SH PERFORMANCE
.PP
Memory usage: ~10 MB for 10,000 files (constant, independent of file sizes)
.PP
Speed: ~10,000 files in <30 seconds on HDD, <10 seconds on SSD
.PP
Parallelization: Use \-\-parallel for 2-3x speedup on multi-core systems
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffa (1),
.BR diffa\-compare (1),
.BR diffa\-verify (1)
